{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefectSubleadingD","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefectSubleadingD","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n1036800D_table","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n1036800D_table","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectSubleadingD.lean#L75-L84","doc":"**Value table — cross-check against the witness.** `n1036800D n = 1036800·D(n)` for\n`n = 2..10`; these integers equal `1036800·` the per-`n` rationals in\n`keystone-wlambda-defect-dn-subleading.witness.json` (held-out `n = 9, 10` PASS). Unlike\n`C(n)`, `D(n)` has no single clean sign flip — it is negative on `2..6`, positive on\n`7..8`, negative on `9..10` (the quartic factor `−100n⁴+1472n³−5273n²−203n−828`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.denom_ladder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.denom_ladder","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectSubleadingD.lean#L65-L73","doc":"**The `144^k` denominator ladder.** Across the defect's coefficient ladder the\ndenominators are `m_k·144^k`: `C(n)` carries `144`, `D(n)` carries `1036800 = 50·144²`,\n`E(n)` carries `21946982400 = 7350·144³` (witness `keystone-wlambda-defect-coeff-ladder`).\nThe Identity-I `144` recurs at every order. Pure `ℤ` arithmetic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n1036800D_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n1036800D_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectSubleadingD.lean#L59-L63","doc":"**Vanishing at the trivial partitions.** `D(n)` carries the same `n(n−1)` factor as\n`C(n) = −n(n−1)(2n−13)/144`, so the `h⁴` defect coefficient vanishes at `n = 0, 1` —\nconsistent with `Z(1) = 1` exactly (no defect for the single-box partition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n1036800D_expanded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n1036800D_expanded","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectSubleadingD.lean#L50-L57","doc":"**Factored = expanded.** The factored form carried in `n1036800D` agrees with the\nwitness's `int_coeffs_low_to_high = [0, 828, −625, 5070, −6745, 1572, −100]`\n(`keystone-wlambda-defect-dn-subleading.witness.json`). Pure ring identity — this is the\nmachine-check that the two forms quoted across the PR/audit are the same polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n1036800D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n1036800D","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectSubleadingD.lean#L43-L48","doc":"`1036800·D(n)` in **factored** form (`1036800 = 50·144²`). `D(n)` is the `h⁴`\ncoefficient of the `W_λ` defect `1 − Z(n)` (companion `C(n)` is the `h²` coefficient).\nStated cleared of the `/1036800` to stay in `ℤ`. Interpolation-derived + held-out\nvalidated; see the file docstring for epistemic status. ","signatureChunk":0}]}